# Auto git snapshot for backtrace

Whenever you install a handoff zip, merge experiment code, wire new arms/campaigns, or finish a delivery round:

1. Stage the relevant new/changed files (code, experiment package, handoffs, scripts). Do not stage secrets, huge unrelated archives from older rounds, or `__pycache__`.
2. Commit with a concise message explaining why (delivery id / experiment id).
3. Push to `fork` remote (`git push fork HEAD:main` or current tracking branch) when a remote is configured.
4. Use prior commit author via `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*` env vars if local git identity is unset — never run `git config`.
5. Do this at the end of the delivery work even if the user does not mention git.
